Probably has some other implications, but it comes out the other end in the desired format, and only if `--test` is present before any positionals. Shockingly, tests are passing (assuming `make test` is the only check).

Note that other test-specific flags suffer from the same issue as the OP described. For example, I may want a 'base' npm run script to run unit tests, but a second npm run script, leveraging the first one, that specifies the `--test-reporter`. My use case: in CI, I want to output test results in Junit XML format for easy storage / analytics / insights in my CI provider. Ideally I could do something like:

