I have proposed a mean to be able able to create Blob / Files with own backing store: https://github.com/w3c/FileAPI/issues/209

The minimum requirement to be able to create Blobs with a own backing store without having to re-implement all logic for arrayBuffer / text / bytes / slice etc is if you provide information about a size and a stream function to be able to create virtual files.

```js
// Creates a virtual blob with own custom backing store
const blob = Blob.from({
  size: 1024,
  async stream(start, end) {
    const rs = fs.createReadStream(path, { start, end })
    return Readable.toWeb(rs)
  }
})

const slicedBlob = blob.slice(10)
slicedBlob.stream() // will call the above stream method with: start: 10, end: 1024
slicedBlob.text() // will call this.stream() internally and also call the above stream

// upgrade the blob to a `File` class
const file = new File([ blob ], filename, {
  type: 'application/octet-stream',
