  uv_run(uvLoop, UV_RUN_NOWAIT);
}
```

`node::CallbackScope` constructs `InternalCallbackScope`, which increments the async callback scope depth via `env->PushAsyncCallbackScope()` (so depth becomes 1 for the whole uv_run call). 

https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/813993b1749d6c48ec868a298368d7644ae8f629/src/api/callback.cc#L91

Because of that, when Node later executes `MakeCallback()` and the JS callback throws, the internal `InternalMakeCallback()` can return an empty `MaybeLocal`. 

Code has a legacy compatibility fallback that converts an empty result into Undefined, but only when the callback scope depth is 0:
https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/813993b1749d6c48ec868a298368d7644ae8f629/src/api/callback.cc#L349-L354

So in our case, that leads to Abort.

