In Node.js version 23, the Diagnostic Report feature is available and can greatly assist with debugging when a process receives a SIGTERM. You can either enable it using the `--diagnostic-report-on-signal` flag or implement a custom SIGTERM handler that generates the report. This report includes a stack trace along with other process details, providing valuable insights into what was happening at the time of termination.

Below is an example of a custom SIGTERM handler:

```javascript
process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  const reportPath = process.report.writeReport();
  console.error(`Diagnostic report generated at: ${reportPath}`);
  process.exit(1);
});
```

This approach generates a detailed diagnostic report at the moment SIGTERM is received, which should help with debugging issues in your application.

