I have been thinking more and more lately about whether it would make sense for `require()` and `import` to include first class support for loading wasm modules.

So instead of...

```js
const obj = await WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming(fetch('test.wasm'))

obj.instance.exports.func();
```

We could essentially have...

```js
const obj = await import('test.wasm');
obj.func();
```

and...

```js
const obj = require('test.wasm');
obj.func();
```

Obviously the `require()` option wouldn't really be that portable outside of Node.js but the import approach as essentially just a wrapper for the WebAssembly boilerplate with caching would make this easier to consume.

