﻿Agreed — `node:stream/consumers` is a very useful but poorly-discoverable module. The main Stream page (https://nodejs.org/api/stream.html) has no mention of it.

The consumers module provides `buffer()`, `text()`, `json()`, and `arrayBuffer()` functions that accept any `ReadableStream` or `async iterable` and collect it fully. These make common stream-to-X patterns trivial:

```js
import { text, json, buffer } from 'node:stream/consumers';

const str = await text(readableStream);
const obj = await json(readableStream);
const buf = await buffer(readableStream);
```

